## Development Workflow

**Starting Development**:
```bash
npm install          # Install dependencies
npm run dev          # Start dev server (http://localhost:3000)
npm run build        # Build for production
npm run preview      # Preview production build
npm run lint         # Run ESLint
```

**Adding a New Page**:
1. Create component in `src/views/[feature]/ComponentName.vue`
2. Add route to `src/router/index.js`
3. Add navigation item to `src/_nav.js` (if needed)
4. Import and use CoreUI components from '@coreui/vue'

**Creating Components with `<script setup>`**:
```vue
<script setup>
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'
import { CCard, CCardBody, CCardHeader } from '@coreui/vue'

// Props
const props = defineProps({
  title: {
    type: String,
    required: true,
  },
  items: {
    type: Array,
    default: () => [],
  },
})

// Emits
const emit = defineEmits(['update', 'delete'])

// State
const isLoading = ref(false)
const selectedItem = ref(null)

// Computed
const itemCount = computed(() => props.items.length)

// Methods
const handleUpdate = () => {
  emit('update', selectedItem.value)
}
</script>

<template>
  <CCard>
    <CCardHeader>{{ title }}</CCardHeader>
    <CCardBody>
      <p>Items: {{ itemCount }}</p>
      <!-- Template content -->
    </CCardBody>
  </CCard>
</template>

<style scoped lang="scss">
// Component-specific styles
</style>
```

**Using Pinia Stores**:
```vue
<script setup>
import { useSidebarStore } from '@/stores/sidebar'
import { useThemeStore } from '@/stores/theme'

const sidebarStore = useSidebarStore()
const themeStore = useThemeStore()

// Access state
console.log(sidebarStore.visible)

// Update state
sidebarStore.toggleSidebar()
themeStore.setTheme('dark')
</script>
```

**Composables Pattern**:
```javascript
// composables/useFetch.js
import { ref } from 'vue'

export function useFetch(url) {
  const data = ref(null)
  const error = ref(null)
  const loading = ref(false)

  const fetchData = async () => {
    loading.value = true
    try {
      const response = await fetch(url)
      data.value = await response.json()
    } catch (e) {
      error.value = e
    } finally {
      loading.value = false
    }
  }

  return { data, error, loading, fetchData }
}
```

## Code Quality

**Linting**:
- ESLint configuration in `eslint.config.mjs`
- Prettier integration for code formatting
- Vue-specific rules with eslint-plugin-vue
- Run `npm run lint` before committing

**Best Practices**:
- Use `<script setup>` for cleaner syntax
- Keep components small and focused
- Extract complex logic into composables
- Use TypeScript JSDoc comments for better IDE support
- Test in both light and dark themes
- Ensure responsive design works on all screen sizes
- Use Vue DevTools for debugging

**Git Commits**:
Follow conventional commit format:
- feat: New feature
- fix: Bug fix
- docs: Documentation changes
- style: Code style changes (formatting)
- refactor: Code refactoring
- test: Adding tests
- chore: Maintenance tasks

## Common Patterns

**Lazy Loading Routes**:
```javascript
const Dashboard = () => import('@/views/dashboard/Dashboard.vue')
```

**Theme Management**:
```vue
<script setup>
import { useColorModes } from '@coreui/vue'

const { colorMode, setColorMode } = useColorModes('coreui-free-vue-admin-template-theme')

// Change theme
setColorMode('dark') // 'light', 'dark', or 'auto'
</script>
```

**Navigation Configuration** (`_nav.js`):
```javascript
export default [
  {
    component: 'CNavItem',
    name: 'Dashboard',
    to: '/dashboard',
    icon: 'cil-speedometer',
    badge: {
      color: 'info',
      text: 'NEW',
    },
  },
  {
    component: 'CNavGroup',
    name: 'Base',
    to: '/base',
    icon: 'cil-puzzle',
    items: [
      {
        component: 'CNavItem',
        name: 'Cards',
        to: '/base/cards',
      },
    ],
  },
]
```

**Pinia Store Definition**:
```javascript
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'
import { defineStore } from 'pinia'

export const useSidebarStore = defineStore('sidebar', () => {
  const visible = ref(true)
  const unfoldable = ref(false)

  const toggleSidebar = () => {
    visible.value = !visible.value
  }

  return { visible, unfoldable, toggleSidebar }
})
```

## AI Assistant Guidelines

**What AI Should Do**:
- Generate code using CoreUI Vue components
- Follow `<script setup>` syntax patterns
- Use Composition API with ref, reactive, computed
- Implement responsive designs
- Follow the project's file organization
- Use existing composables and stores
- Suggest performance optimizations when appropriate
- Add JSDoc comments for complex logic

**What AI Should NOT Do**:
- Use Options API (use Composition API with `<script setup>` instead)
- Import components from libraries other than CoreUI/Vue
- Suggest Tailwind CSS or other CSS frameworks
- Ignore ESLint/Prettier rules
- Create files outside the src/ directory structure
- Modify build configuration without clear reason
- Use deprecated Vue 2 patterns
- Use mixins (use composables instead)

